        "original_id": "afb9ee7e-184f-5d82-b317-9f85f2c6faf4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Modern Records, Modern Music, Flair Records\n- People: Bihari brothers, Little Richard, Etta James, Joe Houston, Ike Turner, Tina Turner, John Lee Hooker\n- Places: Los Angeles\n- Topics: R&B record labels\n\nFacts:\n- In 1945, the Bihari brothers formed Modern Music, an American record company and label, in Los Angeles.\n- Flair Records was a subsidiary of Modern Records.\n- In the 1950s and 1960s, Modern Records was one of the major R&B labels.\n- In the 1950s and 1960s, Modern Records had artists including Etta James, Joe Houston, Little Richard, Ike and Tina Turner, and John Lee Hooker.\n- Richard Wayne Penniman, known as Little Richard, was born on December 5, 1932.\n- Little Richard was an American musician, singer, actor, comedian, and songwriter.",
